MST is really about taking an Undirected graph and removing a few expensive edges so as to maintain the same amount of connectedness with the least weighted edges. So the algorithm below is really about popping off a few heavy edges

MST (Prim's)

// Use a d-Heap or Fibonacci heap

e = find smallest edge // O(E)
push(e)
d = 0;

// where E is max Edges and V is max Vertices
while ((d < (V - 1)) && !empty()) {
    // To pop an edge is to say you care about this edge being in your final MST
    e = pop(); // pop -> min-delete
    --d;
    
    foreach (v : e) {
       if (v !marked) {
       	  v.marked;
	  pushall(v.adjacencylist with weight);
       }
    }
}

// Whatever is left behind in the Queue needs to be popped off and you have yourself a "Minimum Spanning Tree"



